	affiliations = {Universidade Federal de Pelotas, Pelotas, Brazil; Universidade Federal de Pelotas, Departamento de Ciencias Sociales Agrarias, Pelotas, Brazil},
	abstract = {The general objective of this work is to determine the combinations of eco-innovation drivers that favor a high proportion of properties that declare carrying out organic production in Brazilian municipalities. To do so, a theoretical review was carried out that identified 11 drivers, which were then classified as internal and external to agricultural properties. The data were taken from the 2017 Agricultural Census, released by the Brazilian Institute of Geography and Statistics (IBGE). To determine the combinations of drivers associated with organic agricultural production, the qualitative comparative analysis method was used. The results showed that no driver can be defined as necessary. However, two combinations of internal drivers and three combinations of drivers external to rural establishments were determined, sufficient to explain a high proportion of properties dedicated to organic production. These results contribute to the literature on eco-innovation in agriculture and to the monitoring of public policies. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
