	abstract = {Economic growth obeys stimuli from supply and demand. From the supply side, growth depends on the accumulation of factors and their productivity. On the demand side, it is a function of consumption, investment and government spending, and net exports. With the input-output tables, the contributions of the growth of the components of each of the variables can be explained and the growth path followed by the economy can be found. Based on this path, it is judged whether the type of growth is more inclined towards supply or demand. In this paper, the input-output tables are used to demonstrate that the growth experienced in Mexico has been based on a greater dynamic of the supply components, which does not favor the performance of the economic system. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
