	affiliations = {Fundación Ford de la Universidad Mount Holyoke, Holyoke, United States; Economía en la Universidad Mount Holyoke, Holyoke, United States},
	abstract = {Latin America needs higher productivity to escape the middle income trap. In this article, the factors that promote innovation at the company level are analyzed, a key factor to increase productivity. A two-stage model is estimated in which the characteristics of the company affect its use of inputs for innovation; a use that, in turn, generates innovation results. Using data from the 2006, 2010 and 2017 World Bank Business Surveys of five Latin American economies, it is concluded that innovation deficiencies at the aggregate level are not due to the lack of links between innovation inputs and results at the firm level. However, a comparison with companies in China suggests that there may be differences in business conduct. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
